    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "How to read this dashboard",
      "description": "How to read this dashboard.",
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "\n**What it is.** One **GeForce GT 740** (Kepler, compute capability 3.0, 4 GiB) on node `k8s01`, host driver **470** (CUDA 11.4).\nThe **NVIDIA device plugin** advertises it as `nvidia.com/gpu: 1` (handed out exclusively, today to `llm/llama`, which uses\nit through **Vulkan**). **nvidia-gpu-exporter** runs `nvidia-smi` every scrape (no GPU allocation, `utility` capability only).\n\n**Not available on this card:** GPU/memory **utilization**, **power**, **clocks** and **throttle reasons** — nvidia-smi\nreturns *N/A / Not Supported* for them on a GT 740 with driver 470, so the exporter (`--query-field-names AUTO`) does not\nexport them. Use **LLM dashboard → Busy time per second** as the activity signal.\n\n**Healthy looks like:** collection OK, temperature well below 70 °C, VRAM ~1.2 GiB of 4 GiB while llama runs,\nP8 (idle) between requests and P0 while generating, 1 GPU allocatable and 1 allocated (to llama).\n\n**When something goes red:**\n- *Collection* FAILED / stale → `kubectl --context k8s01 -n nvidia-device-plugin logs ds/nvidia-gpu-exporter`; usually the\n  driver (`nvidia-smi` on the host) is broken — see Ansible role `gpu` (homelab-ansible).\n- *Allocatable* 0 → the device plugin lost the GPU (driver/NVML); llama stays Pending after a restart.\n- Temperature ≥ 80 °C → check the fan/airflow; the card slows itself down.\n- VRAM ≥ 95 % → a new model or a bigger context will not fit; llama.cpp falls back to the CPU.\n"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 10
      },
      "id": 2
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "title": "Active alerts for this service",
      "id": 25,
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "description": "Prometheus alerts of this service that are FIRING (condition true for longer than the rule's `for`) or PENDING (condition true, waiting for `for`). Same filter as the red alert annotations of this dashboard; Watchdog/InfoInhibitor are excluded. Empty = healthy. Alertmanager has no receiver in this lab, so dashboards are where alerts are seen: the rule, its threshold and source are in the rule files (helm-charts/<app>/**/prometheus.rules.yaml or the -raw release) and in docs/dashboards/. All alerts of the lab: dashboard \"Alerts overview\" (Observability folder).",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 11,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 5
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "ALERTS{alertname!~\"Watchdog|InfoInhibitor\", alertstate=~\"firing|pending\", namespace=\"nvidia-device-plugin\"}",
          "instant": true,
          "range": false,
          "format": "table"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "align": "auto",
            "cellOptions": {
              "type": "auto"
            }
          },
          "noValue": "No active alerts"
        },
        "overrides": [
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "alertstate"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "displayName",
                "value": "state"
              },
              {
                "id": "custom.cellOptions",
                "value": {
                  "type": "color-background",
                  "mode": "basic"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": "mappings",
                "value": [
                  {
                    "type": "value",
                    "options": {
                      "firing": {
                        "color": "red",
                        "index": 0
                      },
                      "pending": {
                        "color": "orange",
                        "index": 1
                      }
                    }
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "severity"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "custom.cellOptions",
                "value": {
                  "type": "color-text"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": "mappings",
                "value": [
                  {
                    "type": "value",
                    "options": {
                      "critical": {
                        "color": "red",
                        "index": 0
                      },
                      "warning": {
                        "color": "orange",
                        "index": 1
                      },
                      "info": {
                        "color": "blue",
                        "index": 2
                      }
                    }
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "options": {
        "showHeader": true,
        "cellHeight": "sm",
        "footer": {
          "show": false
        }
      },
      "transformations": [
        {
          "id": "organize",
          "options": {
            "excludeByName": {
              "Time": true,
              "Value": true,
              "__name__": true,
              "prometheus": true,
              "endpoint": true,
              "service": true,
              "instance": true,
              "uid": true
            },
            "indexByName": {
              "alertname": 0,
              "alertstate": 1,
              "severity": 2,
              "namespace": 3
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Collection",
      "description": "nvidia_smi_last_collect_success: did the last nvidia-smi run succeed (1) or fail (0). Chart alert NvidiaGpuExporterCollectionFailing fires after 10 min at 0 (https://github.com/utkuozdemir/helm-charts/tree/master/nvidia-gpu-exporter (chart 2.18.0 PrometheusRule)). A failure here means no fresh GPU data at all.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "min(nvidia_smi_last_collect_success{job=\"nvidia-gpu-exporter\"})",
          "legendFormat": "",
          "instant": true,
          "range": false
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          "mappings": [
            {
              "type": "value",
              "options": {
                "0": {
                  "text": "FAILED",
                  "color": "red"
                },
                "1": {
                  "text": "OK",
                  "color": "green"
                }
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "none",
